- **Repeated subjects.** Seahorse appears twice (L5, L51) and koi twice (L76, L89).
- **Weak mid-chapter levels.** A cluster of small or abstract boards has little payoff (L8, L27, L32, L35, L64, L87, L91, L103, L115, L117).
- **Hard concepts taught on soft ground.** Cracked and colour-tally are taught at 66–76% casual, and a few 'bosses' are not harder than the level before them (L30, L54).
- **Hard to read the aha.** The intents are almost all 'chain of fills', so the genuinely clever levels (L4, L9, L24, L46, L82, L101, L108) stand out less than they should.

